  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Between the Estérel massif and the sea, Saint-Raphaël and its surroundings have several family campsites that accept dogs, especially around Fréjus and the Corniche d'Or. The area is handy for reaching the dog-friendly beaches of Fréjus and the red coves of the Estérel.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>As is often the case in this area, the conditions for welcoming dogs (size, breed, supplement) vary from one campsite to another — a direct call before booking is still the safest approach.</p>
      <p>Examples taken from the campsites' own websites and the Saint-Raphaël tourist office listings, all in Agay or Anthéor:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Esterel Caravaning</strong> (5 stars, Agay): according to its own FAQ, dogs of all sizes are accepted on pitches and in mobile homes, with no restriction on breed or category (categories 1 and 2 included), with a €5 per night surcharge in high season only; dogs on a leash in common areas and not allowed in the pools.</li>
        <li><strong>Les Mas de l'Estérel</strong> (3-star holiday village, Agay): "dogs accepted outside July-August", with a surcharge, according to the tourist office.</li>
        <li><strong>Azur Rivage</strong> (2-star campsite, Anthéor): animals accepted with a surcharge, including in rentals, according to the tourist office; open from 1 May to 30 September 2026.</li>
        <li><strong>Agay Soleil</strong> (campsite, Agay): animals accepted with a surcharge according to the tourist office; a third-party campsite guide (HPA Guide) says they are not allowed in the rentals: ask before booking a mobile home.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: in Saint-Raphaël itself, dogs are allowed on specific stretches of coastline between certain beaches — check the exact zones before settling on the sand.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Argens beach in Fréjus, with its year-round dog zone, is a few minutes' drive away.</p>
    </div>

